{"title":"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jarek multiplies a number by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and gets an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If instead, he divides the number by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, what answer does he get?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c5aae0c291c7bc4b558b429a9234d9aab776a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 30 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 60 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 270$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number that Jarek multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using the first sentence, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d711dc3e4b767cb31c2c0d5419968ed197da85b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3cbc01b2d2b1cd07002c305521aaf884a3b43de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 30$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>We are then looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c7484459d6015b7c6e842ab64f81623b37d5e093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\div 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/344ca80d458fb7a25b1afe0ee8a5bcda97fdaa02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\div 3 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without finding the number that Jarek multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b2b95bdc470c2ae10889f443f863aeb8e642626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\div 3 = 3x \\div 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, we can divide the product by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679e00f52ddeea812dc37fe8915b387740ca463d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 \\div 9 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1